## Problem statement

When I use this schema:
```json
  "definitions" : {
    "Resource" : {
      "type" : "object",
      "required" : [ "sourceId", "title" ],
      "additionalProperties" : true,
      "properties" : {
        "id" : {
          "type" : "string",
          "example" : "oo000oo0001"
        },
        "title" : {
          "type" : "string",
          "example" : "My work"
        },
        "sourceId" : {
          "type" : "string",
          "example" : "bib12345678"
        }
      }
  }
```

and I don't provide a `sourceId` in the request, then it doesn't return a validation error.  If I remove the `additionalProperties: true` then it does return an error.

## Swagger specification
2.0

## Steps to reproduce

## Environment
swagger version: 0.13.0  
go version: 1.9  
OS:  osX

